  "details": "I wonder if it could be possible to use face tracking tech\n\nto readjust the players camera lighting when they walk into \n\ndark spaces as a eyes naturally do in low light conditions \n\ncoming from bright light conditions for vr headsets.\n\nso the camera will adjust based on how your eyes need to adjust on darker or brighter areas, \n\neven if the tech was slow it could make a big difference for some and help horror game maps experience.\n\nthe idea came along when the lights went off in a world and \n\nI was trapped and my eyes cant make the vr headset adjust to the \n\nnew low lighting, with eye tracking I think this will be very possible.",
